# Hi, I’m Sunn789 👋

## Backend & Full-Stack Software Developer

I design and build business applications, APIs, websites, dashboards, mobile apps, and practical AI/data experiments. My main professional direction is **.NET backend and full-stack development**, with additional hands-on work in **Flutter/Dart**, **Angular**, and **Python computer vision and speech processing**.

I enjoy turning real business requirements into maintainable software: modeling the domain, designing secure APIs, implementing workflows, connecting data, and delivering a usable interface.

## Main application: Accountant3 / YAccountant

[View Accountant3 on GitHub →](https://github.com/sunn789/accountant3)

Accountant3 is my main and most complete application: a financial and administrative management platform for budgets, expenses, organizational centers, users, approvals, and reporting.

### What I developed

- A secure ASP.NET Core API for budget allocations, adjustments, expenses, items, centers, users, dashboards, reports, and payments
- Financial workflows including monthly expense registration, editing, approval, deletion, debt details, budget locking, and yearly summaries
- Role- and center-aware authorization for administrators, accountants, and users restricted to their own organizational center
- JWT authentication, ASP.NET Core Identity, roles, claims, authorization policies, and refresh-token-related domain support
- Health-check endpoints, database initialization, migrations, validation, pagination, centralized API responses, and OpenAPI/Scalar documentation
- An Angular UI with authenticated routing, lazy-loaded features, route guards, role guards, HTTP authentication interceptors, dashboards, user management, centers, and budget allocation screens
- A Razor Pages UI for server-rendered administration and financial workflows

### Architecture and engineering

Accountant3 is organized using **Clean Architecture** principles, with clear boundaries between the API, Application, Core/Domain, Infrastructure, Contracts, and UI layers. Application features follow a **Vertical Slice / feature-oriented structure**, keeping commands, queries, handlers, validators, DTOs, mappings, and related behavior close to the use case they implement.

The project demonstrates my ability to work with:

`C#` `ASP.NET Core` `.NET 10` `MediatR` `CQRS` `Entity Framework Core` `SQL Server` `SQLite` `ASP.NET Core Identity` `JWT` `FluentValidation` `AutoMapper` `Angular` `TypeScript` `Razor Pages` `OpenAPI`

